# Kapp's Dev Planner Bundle

Plan projects before building them: `/dev-planner` runs drill-me → PRD → tasks → plan with a
gate between steps; each step is also its own skill. Artifacts live in `docs/planning/`
(`00-brief.md`, `01-prd.md`, `02-tasks.md`, `03-plan.md`). Project memory lives in a local
Rta-Smriti brain; read it with the `rta-smriti` MCP tools (`brain_context_pack` first) and
write with `scripts/brain.sh` from the plugin.

Recommendation: run the coding agent from a terminal CLI (Claude Code, Grok Build, Cursor's
CLI agent) for the best system vision. A CLI host can scan the machine, install toolchains,
bootstrap the brain, and run verification commands. In an IDE chat pane without a shell,
the machine-scan and install steps of `/drill-me` are degraded; the skill will say so and
give the command to run from a CLI.

Cursor note: there is no `$ARGUMENTS`; the text typed after `/drill-me` is the input.
